{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786433711755,"sessionID":"ses_010495b2effeRJw5ynhosNr3HY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"grep","callID":"call_00_7rAJX9ABkxcIFHBBKU9U7981","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"MessageDisplay|message_id|transcript_path|displayContent|suppressOutput","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_fefbede7e001z2FlWRpdv6qHp0"},"output":"Found 100 matches (more matches available)\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_fefbb910f001NR6DpjGu7rHShh:\n  Line 27:     <img src=\"https://mintcdn.com/claude-code/jhXrDR5TrSZ5hgXM/images/hooks-lifecycle.svg?fit=max&auto=format&n=jhXrDR5TrSZ5hgXM&q=85&s=3ca47113d5956460e6e4611b8dbc63b7\" className=\"dark:hidden\" alt=\"Hook lifecycle diagram showing optional Setup feeding into SessionStart, then a per-turn loop containing UserPromptSubmit, UserPromptExpansion for slash commands, the nested agentic loop (PreToolUse, PermissionRequest, PostToolUse, PostToolUseFailure, PostToolBatch, SubagentStart/Stop, TaskCreated, TaskCompleted), and Stop or StopFailure, followed by TeammateIdle, PreCompact, PostCompact, and SessionEnd, with Elicitation and ElicitationResult nested inside MCP tool execution, PermissionDenied as a side branch from PermissionRequest for auto-mode denials, WorktreeCreate, WorktreeRemove, Notification, ConfigChange, InstructionsLoaded, CwdChanged, FileChanged, and DirectoryAdded as standalone async events, and MessageDisplay as a display-only event that runs while assistant message text streams\" width=\"520\" height=\"1228\" data-path=\"images/hooks-lifecycle.svg\" />\n\n  Line 29:     <img src=\"https://mintcdn.com/claude-code/jhXrDR5TrSZ5hgXM/images/hooks-lifecycle-dark.svg?fit=max&auto=format&n=jhXrDR5TrSZ5hgXM&q=85&s=0ffe95014d33411538778a66e4173973\" className=\"hidden dark:block\" alt=\"Hook lifecycle diagram showing optional Setup feeding into SessionStart, then a per-turn loop containing UserPromptSubmit, UserPromptExpansion for slash commands, the nested agentic loop (PreToolUse, PermissionRequest, PostToolUse, PostToolUseFailure, PostToolBatch, SubagentStart/Stop, TaskCreated, TaskCompleted), and Stop or StopFailure, followed by TeammateIdle, PreCompact, PostCompact, and SessionEnd, with Elicitation and ElicitationResult nested inside MCP tool execution, PermissionDenied as a side branch from PermissionRequest for auto-mode denials, WorktreeCreate, WorktreeRemove, Notification, ConfigChange, InstructionsLoaded, CwdChanged, FileChanged, and DirectoryAdded as standalone async events, and MessageDisplay as a display-only event that runs while assistant message text streams\" width=\"520\" height=\"1228\" data-path=\"images/hooks-lifecycle-dark.svg\" />\n\n  Line 48: | `MessageDisplay`      | While assistant message text is displayed                                                                                                              |\n\n  Line 316: | `UserPromptSubmit`, `PostToolBatch`, `Stop`, `TeammateIdle`, `TaskCreated`, `TaskCompleted`, `WorktreeCreate`, `WorktreeRemove`, `MessageDisplay` | no matcher support                                           | always fires on every occurrence                                                                                                                                                           |\n\n  Line 415: | `timeout`       | no       | Seconds before canceling. Defaults: 600 for `command`, `http`, and `mcp_tool`; 30 for `prompt`; 60 for `agent`. [`UserPromptSubmit`](#userpromptsubmit) lowers the `command`, `http`, and `mcp_tool` default to 30, and [`MessageDisplay`](#messagedisplay) lowers it to 10. [`SessionEnd`](#sessionend) hooks share a 1.5-second budget; if your settings set a longer per-hook `timeout`, Claude Code raises the budget to match, up to 60 seconds                                                                                            |\n\n  Line 704: | `transcript_path` | Path to conversation JSON. The transcript file is written asynchronously and may lag the in-memory conversation, so it may not yet include the current turn's most recent messages when a hook fires. Hooks that need the final assistant text of the current turn should use `last_assistant_message` on [Stop](#stop) and [SubagentStop](#subagentstop) instead of reading the transcript                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n\n  Line 725:   \"transcript_path\": \"/home/user/.claude/projects/.../transcript.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 812: | `MessageDisplay`      | No         | The original text is displayed                                                                                                                 |\n\n  Line 850: | `suppressOutput`   | `false` | If `true`, hides the hook's stdout from the transcript. Stdout still appears in the debug log                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n\n  Line 946: | MessageDisplay                                                                                                                      | `hookSpecificOutput`           | `displayContent` replaces the displayed text on screen. Display-only: the transcript and what Claude sees keep the original                                                                                                         |\n\n  Line 1044:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1074: Since plain stdout already reaches Claude for this event, a hook that only loads context can print to stdout directly without building JSON. Use the JSON form when you need to combine context with other fields such as `suppressOutput` or `sessionTitle`.\n\n  Line 1158:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1208:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../transcript.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1240:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1296:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../00893aaf.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1329: ### MessageDisplay\n\n  Line 1333: Use MessageDisplay to:\n\n  Line 1341: MessageDisplay is display-only: the replacement text changes only what is rendered on screen. The transcript and what Claude sees keep the original text, so Claude never sees the replacement, and verbose mode shows the original. The hook receives assistant message text only, so tool results and the text you type render unchanged.\n\n  Line 1343: MessageDisplay doesn't support matchers and fires for every assistant message that streams text; messages with no text, such as tool-call-only responses, don't trigger it.\n\n  Line 1345: In non-interactive runs, including Agent SDK queries and `claude -p`, MessageDisplay runs once per assistant message instead of once per batch of lines. The single call arrives after the message completes and carries the full message text: `index` is `0`, `final` is `true`, and `delta` holds the entire message. A hook that collects the `delta` text for each message receives the same total text in both modes.\n\n  Line 1347: #### MessageDisplay input\n\n  Line 1349: In addition to the [common input fields](#common-input-fields), MessageDisplay hooks receive identifiers for the turn and message, the position of this call within the message, and the new text in `delta`. Batch boundaries depend on how the text streams, so use `index` and `final` to track progress through a message rather than expecting lines to be grouped a particular way.\n\n  Line 1354: | `message_id` | UUID of the assistant message being displayed. Stable across every batch of the same message. This is not the API `msg_…` id, so it can't be correlated with transcript message ids                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n\n  Line 1362:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../transcript.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1364:   \"hook_event_name\": \"MessageDisplay\",\n\n  Line 1366:   \"message_id\": \"5b2a9c8e-1f63-4d8a-b7c4-9e0d2a6f1c3b\",\n\n  Line 1373: #### MessageDisplay output\n\n  Line 1375: In addition to the [JSON output fields](#json-output) available to all hooks, MessageDisplay hooks can return `displayContent` to replace the delta on screen:\n\n  Line 1379: | `displayContent` | Text displayed in place of the delta. Omit it to display the original |\n\n  Line 1381: MessageDisplay hooks have no decision control. They can't block the message or change what is stored in the transcript or sent to Claude.\n\n  Line 1383: This example strips markdown formatting from Claude's responses for a plain-text display. The script reads each batch from stdin, removes bold markers and inline code backticks from `delta`, and returns the result as `displayContent`.\n\n  Line 1392:         \"MessageDisplay\": [\n\n  Line 1411:     jq '{hookSpecificOutput: {hookEventName: \"MessageDisplay\", displayContent: (.delta | gsub(\"\\\\*\\\\*\"; \"\") | gsub(\"`\"; \"\"))}}'\n\n  Line 1421:         \"MessageDisplay\": [\n\n  Line 1451:         hookEventName = \"MessageDisplay\"\n\n  Line 1452:         displayContent = $text\n\n  Line 1752:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1839:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1913:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1969:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2028:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2125:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2149:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2178: In addition to the [common input fields](#common-input-fields), SubagentStop hooks receive `stop_hook_active`, `agent_id`, `agent_type`, `agent_transcript_path`, and `last_assistant_message`. The `agent_type` field is the value used for matcher filtering. The `transcript_path` is the main session's transcript, while `agent_transcript_path` is the subagent's own transcript stored in a nested `subagents/` folder. The `last_assistant_message` field contains the text content of the subagent's final response, so hooks can access it without parsing the transcript file.\n\n  Line 2185:   \"transcript_path\": \"~/.claude/projects/.../abc123.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2192:   \"agent_transcript_path\": \"~/.claude/projects/.../abc123/subagents/agent-def456.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2214:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2269:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2326: The `last_assistant_message` field contains the text content of Claude's final response, so hooks can access it without parsing the transcript file. For hooks that act on the just-completed turn, such as read-aloud or notification hooks, use this field rather than reading `transcript_path`: the transcript file isn't guaranteed to include the final message at Stop time on all versions.\n\n  Line 2358:   \"transcript_path\": \"~/.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2429:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2453:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2530:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2571:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../transcript.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2622:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../transcript.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2658:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../transcript.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2712:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2770:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2801:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2827:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2860:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2890:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2911:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 2958:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/.local/share/opencode/tool-output/tool_fefbede7e001z2FlWRpdv6qHp0:\n  Line 27:     <img src=\"https://mintcdn.com/claude-code/jhXrDR5TrSZ5hgXM/images/hooks-lifecycle.svg?fit=max&auto=format&n=jhXrDR5TrSZ5hgXM&q=85&s=3ca47113d5956460e6e4611b8dbc63b7\" className=\"dark:hidden\" alt=\"Hook lifecycle diagram showing optional Setup feeding into SessionStart, then a per-turn loop containing UserPromptSubmit, UserPromptExpansion for slash commands, the nested agentic loop (PreToolUse, PermissionRequest, PostToolUse, PostToolUseFailure, PostToolBatch, SubagentStart/Stop, TaskCreated, TaskCompleted), and Stop or StopFailure, followed by TeammateIdle, PreCompact, PostCompact, and SessionEnd, with Elicitation and ElicitationResult nested inside MCP tool execution, PermissionDenied as a side branch from PermissionRequest for auto-mode denials, WorktreeCreate, WorktreeRemove, Notification, ConfigChange, InstructionsLoaded, CwdChanged, FileChanged, and DirectoryAdded as standalone async events, and MessageDisplay as a display-only event that runs while assistant message text streams\" width=\"520\" height=\"1228\" data-path=\"images/hooks-lifecycle.svg\" />\n\n  Line 29:     <img src=\"https://mintcdn.com/claude-code/jhXrDR5TrSZ5hgXM/images/hooks-lifecycle-dark.svg?fit=max&auto=format&n=jhXrDR5TrSZ5hgXM&q=85&s=0ffe95014d33411538778a66e4173973\" className=\"hidden dark:block\" alt=\"Hook lifecycle diagram showing optional Setup feeding into SessionStart, then a per-turn loop containing UserPromptSubmit, UserPromptExpansion for slash commands, the nested agentic loop (PreToolUse, PermissionRequest, PostToolUse, PostToolUseFailure, PostToolBatch, SubagentStart/Stop, TaskCreated, TaskCompleted), and Stop or StopFailure, followed by TeammateIdle, PreCompact, PostCompact, and SessionEnd, with Elicitation and ElicitationResult nested inside MCP tool execution, PermissionDenied as a side branch from PermissionRequest for auto-mode denials, WorktreeCreate, WorktreeRemove, Notification, ConfigChange, InstructionsLoaded, CwdChanged, FileChanged, and DirectoryAdded as standalone async events, and MessageDisplay as a display-only event that runs while assistant message text streams\" width=\"520\" height=\"1228\" data-path=\"images/hooks-lifecycle-dark.svg\" />\n\n  Line 48: | `MessageDisplay`      | While assistant message text is displayed                                                                                                              |\n\n  Line 316: | `UserPromptSubmit`, `PostToolBatch`, `Stop`, `TeammateIdle`, `TaskCreated`, `TaskCompleted`, `WorktreeCreate`, `WorktreeRemove`, `MessageDisplay` | no matcher support                                           | always fires on every occurrence                                                                                                                                                           |\n\n  Line 415: | `timeout`       | no       | Seconds before canceling. Defaults: 600 for `command`, `http`, and `mcp_tool`; 30 for `prompt`; 60 for `agent`. [`UserPromptSubmit`](#userpromptsubmit) lowers the `command`, `http`, and `mcp_tool` default to 30, and [`MessageDisplay`](#messagedisplay) lowers it to 10. [`SessionEnd`](#sessionend) hooks share a 1.5-second budget; if your settings set a longer per-hook `timeout`, Claude Code raises the budget to match, up to 60 seconds                                                                                            |\n\n  Line 704: | `transcript_path` | Path to conversation JSON. The transcript file is written asynchronously and may lag the in-memory conversation, so it may not yet include the current turn's most recent messages when a hook fires. Hooks that need the final assistant text of the current turn should use `last_assistant_message` on [Stop](#stop) and [SubagentStop](#subagentstop) instead of reading the transcript                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                      |\n\n  Line 725:   \"transcript_path\": \"/home/user/.claude/projects/.../transcript.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 812: | `MessageDisplay`      | No         | The original text is displayed                                                                                                                 |\n\n  Line 850: | `suppressOutput`   | `false` | If `true`, hides the hook's stdout from the transcript. Stdout still appears in the debug log                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |\n\n  Line 946: | MessageDisplay                                                                                                                      | `hookSpecificOutput`           | `displayContent` replaces the displayed text on screen. Display-only: the transcript and what Claude sees keep the original                                                                                                         |\n\n  Line 1044:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1074: Since plain stdout already reaches Claude for this event, a hook that only loads context can print to stdout directly without building JSON. Use the JSON form when you need to combine context with other fields such as `suppressOutput` or `sessionTitle`.\n\n  Line 1158:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1208:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../transcript.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1240:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../00893aaf-19fa-41d2-8238-13269b9b3ca0.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1296:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../00893aaf.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1329: ### MessageDisplay\n\n  Line 1333: Use MessageDisplay to:\n\n  Line 1341: MessageDisplay is display-only: the replacement text changes only what is rendered on screen. The transcript and what Claude sees keep the original text, so Claude never sees the replacement, and verbose mode shows the original. The hook receives assistant message text only, so tool results and the text you type render unchanged.\n\n  Line 1343: MessageDisplay doesn't support matchers and fires for every assistant message that streams text; messages with no text, such as tool-call-only responses, don't trigger it.\n\n  Line 1345: In non-interactive runs, including Agent SDK queries and `claude -p`, MessageDisplay runs once per assistant message instead of once per batch of lines. The single call arrives after the message completes and carries the full message text: `index` is `0`, `final` is `true`, and `delta` holds the entire message. A hook that collects the `delta` text for each message receives the same total text in both modes.\n\n  Line 1347: #### MessageDisplay input\n\n  Line 1349: In addition to the [common input fields](#common-input-fields), MessageDisplay hooks receive identifiers for the turn and message, the position of this call within the message, and the new text in `delta`. Batch boundaries depend on how the text streams, so use `index` and `final` to track progress through a message rather than expecting lines to be grouped a particular way.\n\n  Line 1354: | `message_id` | UUID of the assistant message being displayed. Stable across every batch of the same message. This is not the API `msg_…` id, so it can't be correlated with transcript message ids                                                                                                                                                                                                               |\n\n  Line 1362:   \"transcript_path\": \"/Users/.../.claude/projects/.../transcript.jsonl\",\n\n  Line 1364:   \"hook_event_name\": \"MessageDisplay\",\n\n  Line 1366:   \"message_id\": \"5b2a9c8e-1f63-4d8a-b7c4-9e0d2a6f1c3b\",\n\n  Line 1373: #### MessageDisplay output\n\n  Line 1375: In addition to the [JSON output fields](#json-output) available to all hooks, MessageDisplay hooks can return `displayContent` to replace the delta on screen:\n\n  Line 1379: | `displayContent` | Text displayed in place of the delta. Omit it to display the original |\n\n  Line 1381: MessageDisplay hooks have no decision control. They can't block the message or change what is stored in the transcript or sent to Claude.\n\n  Line 1383: This example strips markdown formatting from Claude's responses for a plain-text display. The script reads each batch from stdin, removes bold markers and inline code backticks from `delta`, and returns the result as `displayContent`.\n\n  Line 1392:         \"MessageDisplay\": [\n\n  Line 1411:     jq '{hookSpecificOutput: {hookEventName: \"MessageDisplay\", displayContent: (.delta | gsub(\"\\\\*\\\\*\"; \"\") | gsub(\"`\"; \"\"))}}'\n\n  Line 1421:         \"MessageDisplay\": [\n\n\n(Results truncated. Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","metadata":{"matches":100,"truncated":true},"title":"MessageDisplay|message_id|transcript_path|displayContent|suppressOutput","time":{"start":1786433711730,"end":1786433711753}},"id":"prt_fefbf2cc9001hGCVBhebvHgNLl","sessionID":"ses_010495b2effeRJw5ynhosNr3HY","messageID":"msg_fefbee369001qO1Z15QuTIYfA8"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1786433712311,"sessionID":"ses_010495b2effeRJw5ynhosNr3HY","part":{"id":"prt_fefbf2bf7001JLzQ058konxKvP","messageID":"msg_fefbee369001qO1Z15QuTIYfA8","sessionID":"ses_010495b2effeRJw5ynhosNr3HY","type":"text","text":"I have substantial primary-source evidence. Let me extract the key MessageDisplay-specific facts from the fetched hook docs.","time":{"start":1786433711095,"end":1786433712308}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1786433712861,"sessionID":"ses_010495b2effeRJw5ynhosNr3HY","part":{"id":"prt_fefbf32da001W4uucFzgarIaTg","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"294698843c2769f52bad227eec6fe123edf49de0","messageID":"msg_fefbee369001qO1Z15QuTIYfA8","sessionID":"ses_010495b2effeRJw5ynhosNr3HY","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":219969,"input":23044,"output":132,"reasoning":57,"cache":{"write":0,"read":196736}},"cost":0.0019149704}}
