st integration boundary in each of the six CLIs (Claude CLI, Codex CLI, Pi CLI, OpenCode CLI, Devin CLI, Cursor CLI) for display-only projection?\n - [x] Q3: What normalized event and message model preserves canonical transcript, model context, tool events, and streaming behavior across all six runtimes?\n - [ ] Q4: What streaming, buffering, ordering, concurrency, cancellation, and retry semantics must the portable assembler honor?\n-- [ ] Q5: How should protected spans be encoded and fidelity validated so the system can objectively reject bad rewrites and fall back to the exact original?\n+- [x] Q5: How should protected spans be encoded and fidelity validated so the system can objectively reject bad rewrites and fall back to the exact original?\n - [x] Q6: What provider-neutral configuration (protocol, base URL, model, auth, privacy class, cost, capability, fallback) supports OpenCode Go DeepSeek V4 Flash and local Ollama/llama.cpp with privacy-aware routing?\n - [ ] Q7: What observability and evaluation methods objectively measure perceptual 1:1 communication parity?\n - [ ] Q8: What downstream phase decomposition and handoff evidence should follow this research phase?\n <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n","filediff":{"file":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0138-system-deep-loop-communication-research/specs/cli-external-orchestration/042-improved-communication/001-research-strategy/research/lineages/deepseek-go/deep-research-strategy.md","patch":"Index: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0138-system-deep-loop-communication-research/specs/cli-external-orchestration/042-improved-communication/001-research-strategy/research/lineages/deepseek-go/deep-research-strategy.md\n===================================================================\n--- /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0138-system-deep-loop-communication-research/specs/cli-external-orchestration/042-improved-communication/001-research-strategy/research/lineages/deepseek-go/deep-research-strategy.md\n+++ /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0138-system-deep-loop-communication-research/specs/cli-external-orchestration/042-improved-communication/001-research-strategy/research/lineages/deepseek-go/deep-research-strategy.md\n@@ -37,9 +37,9 @@\n - [x] Q1: What is the exact claudish-to-english architecture (hooks, buffering, context, prompt, provider call, display modes, cleanup, failure paths) with file-and-line evidence?\n - [x] Q2: What is the safest integration boundary in each of the six CLIs (Claude CLI, Codex CLI, Pi CLI, OpenCode CLI, Devin CLI, Cursor CLI) for display-only projection?\n - [x] Q3: What normalized event and message model preserves canonical transcript, model context, tool events, and streaming behavior across all six runtimes?\n - [ ] Q4: What streaming, buffering, ordering, concurrency, cancellation, and retry semantics must the portable assembler honor?\n-- [ ] Q5: How should protected spans be encoded and fidelity validated so the system can objectively reject bad rewrites and fall back to the exact original?\n+- [x] Q5: How should protected spans be encoded and fidelity validated so the system can objectively reject bad rewrites and fall back to the exact original?\n - [x] Q6: What provider-neutral configuration (protocol, base URL, model, auth, privacy class, cost, capability, fallback) supports OpenCode Go DeepSeek V4 Flash and local Ollama/llama.cpp with privacy-aware routing?\n - [ ] Q7: What observability and evaluation methods objectively measure perceptual 1:1 communication parity?\n - [ ] Q8: What downstream phase decomposition and handoff evidence should follow this research phase?\n <!-- /ANCHOR:key-questions -->\n","additions":1,"deletions":1},"truncated":false},"title":"specs/cli-external-orchestration/042-improved-communication/001-research-strategy/research/lineages/deep