{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1786434757603,"sessionID":"ses_010495b2effeRJw5ynhosNr3HY","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_00_ET_5uFF2QdEM2BKpWDxLnJJ5645","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0138-system-deep-loop-communication-research/specs/cli-external-orchestration/042-improved-communication/001-research-strategy/research/lineages/deepseek-go/deep-research-strategy.md","limit":18,"offset":36},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0138-system-deep-loop-communication-research/specs/cli-external-orchestration/042-improved-communication/001-research-strategy/research/lineages/deepseek-go/deep-research-strategy.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n36: \n37: - [x] Q1: What is the exact claudish-to-english architecture (hooks, buffering, context, prompt, provider call, display modes, cleanup, failure paths) with file-and-line evidence?\n38: - [x] Q2: What is the safest integration boundary in each of the six CLIs (Claude CLI, Codex CLI, Pi CLI, OpenCode CLI, Devin CLI, Cursor CLI) for display-only projection?\n39: - [x] Q3: What normalized event and message model preserves canonical transcript, model context, tool events, and streaming behavior across all six runtimes?\n40: - [ ] Q4: What streaming, buffering, ordering, concurrency, cancellation, and retry semantics must the portable assembler honor?\n41: - [x] Q5: How should protected spans be encoded and fidelity validated so the system can objectively reject bad rewrites and fall back to the exact original?\n42: - [x] Q6: What provider-neutral configuration (protocol, base URL, model, auth, privacy class, cost, capability, fallback) supports OpenCode Go DeepSeek V4 Flash and local Ollama/llama.cpp with privacy-aware routing?\n43: - [ ] Q7: What observability and evaluation methods objectively measure perceptual 1:1 communication parity?\n44: - [ ] Q8: